{"id": "EUVD-2026-101224", "enisaUuid": "5c348718-4729-30c7-8a2a-73a747367cd5", "description": "quirc through 1.2 contains an excessive-iteration vulnerability in find_alignment_pattern() in lib/identify.c that allows attackers to hang quirc_end() with a crafted image. Attackers can arrange three finder patterns producing a near-degenerate perspective transform, causing billions of region_code() iterations that exhaust CPU in applications decoding attacker-supplied QR images.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T01:02:45", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/dlbeer/quirc/pull/159", "https://github.com/dlbeer/quirc/issues/162", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/quirc-alignment-pattern-infinite-loop-dos", "https://github.com/dlbeer/quirc/blob/542848dd6b9b0eaa9587bbf25b9bc67bd8a71fca/lib/identify.c#L578-L636", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/quirc-through-1.2-denial-of-service-via-find-alignment-pattern-spiral-search"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fjm5-xm8f-3gjj", "CVE-2026-110596"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b3fa9bc7-f10a-3ca0-bc0d-817bf7b2ce07", "product": {"name": "quirc", "vendor": {"name": "dlbeer"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "65aa3ec9-6aa7-3889-b873-a8eac8ca3fe7", "vendor": {"name": "dlbeer"}}], "isExploited": false}